## 3. LITELEMENT BASICS

### 3.1 Minimal Component

```typescript
// my-greeting.ts
import { LitElement, html } from 'lit';
import { customElement, property } from 'lit/decorators.js';

@customElement('my-greeting')
export class MyGreeting extends LitElement {
  @property() name = 'World';

  render() {
    return html`<h1>Hello, ${this.name}!</h1>`;
  }
}

// Declare for TypeScript
declare global {
  interface HTMLElementTagNameMap {
    'my-greeting': MyGreeting;
  }
}
```

```html
<!-- Usage -->
<my-greeting name="Lit"></my-greeting>
<!-- Renders: <h1>Hello, Lit!</h1> -->
```

### 3.2 Without Decorators (Vanilla JS)

```javascript
// my-greeting.js (no TypeScript, no decorators)
import { LitElement, html } from 'lit';

export class MyGreeting extends LitElement {
