## 6. STYLES & CSS

### 6.1 Static Styles

```typescript
import { LitElement, css } from 'lit';

@customElement('styled-element')
export class StyledElement extends LitElement {
  // Preferred: static styles (parsed once, shared across instances)
  static styles = css`
    :host {
      display: block;
      padding: 16px;
      border: 1px solid #ccc;
      border-radius: 8px;
      font-family: sans-serif;
    }

    :host([hidden]) {
      display: none;
    }

    :host([active]) {
      border-color: blue;
    }

    :host(:hover) {
      box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      color: var(--heading-color, #333);
    }

    p {
      color: var(--text-color, #666);
    }

    ::slotted(span) {
      font-weight: bold;        /* Style slotted light DOM */
    }

    ::slotted(*) {
      margin: 4px 0;
    }
  `;

  render() {
    return html`
      <h2><slot name="title">Default Title</slot></h2>
      <p><slot></slot></p>
    `;
  }
}
```

### 6.2 CSS Selectors in Shadow DOM

| Selector | Target |
|----------|--------|
| `:host` | The component element itself |
| `:host(.class)` | The host when it has a class |
| `:host([attr])` | The host when it has an attribute |
| `:host(:hover)` | The host in pseudo-state |
| `:host-context(.theme-dark)` | Host when ancestor matches |
| `::slotted(selector)` | Light DOM children in slots |
| `:host > *` | Direct children in shadow DOM |
| `*` | All shadow DOM elements |

### 6.3 Multiple Style Sheets

```typescript
// Array of styles (last one wins for conflicts)
