## 20. PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION

### 20.1 Performance Best Practices

```
Performance Checklist:
├── Rendering
│   ├── Use static styles (parsed once, shared via constructable stylesheets)
│   ├── Use `nothing` instead of empty string for conditional rendering
│   ├── Use `repeat()` with keys for large reordering lists
│   ├── Use `.map()` for simple append-only lists (lighter than repeat)
│   ├── Use `guard()` to skip expensive re-renders
│   ├── Use `cache()` to preserve DOM for toggled views
│   ├── Avoid large inline templates — break into methods
│   └── Use `willUpdate()` for derived state (not `updated()`)
│
├── Properties
│   ├── Use `attribute: false` for complex objects (skip serialization)
│   ├── Prefer @state for internal data (no attribute overhead)
│   ├── Avoid reflecting complex properties (reflect: false)
│   └── Create new references for objects/arrays (immutable updates)
│
├── Events
│   ├── Use event delegation for lists
│   ├── Use `{ passive: true }` for scroll/touch handlers
│   └── Clean up listeners in disconnectedCallback
│
├── Loading
│   ├── Lazy-load child components with dynamic import()
│   ├── Use code splitting per route
│   └── Tree-shake unused directives
│
└── Measurement
    ├── Use Chrome DevTools Performance tab
    ├── Use Lighthouse for audits
    └── Profile with Performance.mark/measure
```

### 20.2 Lazy Loading Components

```typescript
@customElement('lazy-app')
export class LazyApp extends LitElement {
  @state() private _page = 'home';

  render() {
    return html`
      <nav>
        <button @click=${() => this._loadPage('home')}>Home</button>
        <button @click=${() => this._loadPage('dashboard')}>Dashboard</button>
        <button @click=${() => this._loadPage('settings')}>Settings</button>
      </nav>
      <main>${this._renderPage()}</main>
    `;
  }

  private async _loadPage(page: string) {
    // Dynamically import component only when needed
    switch (page) {
      case 'dashboard':
        await import('./pages/dashboard-page.js');
        break;
      case 'settings':
        await import('./pages/settings-page.js');
        break;
    }
    this._page = page;
  }

  private _renderPage() {
    switch (this._page) {
      case 'home':      return html`<home-page></home-page>`;
      case 'dashboard': return html`<dashboard-page></dashboard-page>`;
      case 'settings':  return html`<settings-page></settings-page>`;
      default:          return html`<p>Not found</p>`;
    }
  }
}
