| **Size** | ~5 KB | ~40 KB | ~33 KB | ~150 KB | ~2 KB (runtime) |
| **Rendering** | lit-html (tagged templates) | Virtual DOM (JSX) | Virtual DOM (SFC) | Change Detection | Compiled DOM ops |
| **Reactivity** | Property-based | useState/hooks | Proxy-based | Zone.js / Signals | Compiled reactivity |
| **Scoping** | Shadow DOM (native) | CSS Modules / CSS-in-JS | Scoped styles | ViewEncapsulation | Scoped styles |
| **Interop** | Excellent (standard) | Moderate | Moderate | Moderate | Moderate |
| **Learning Curve** | Low | Medium | Medium | High | Low |
| **Ecosystem** | Small but growing | Massive | Large | Large | Growing |
| **SSR** | Experimental | Mature (Next.js) | Mature (Nuxt) | Universal | Mature (SvelteKit) |
| **Mobile** | Via PWA | React Native | Via Capacitor | Via Ionic | Via Capacitor |
| **State Mgmt** | Controllers, Context | Redux, Zustand | Pinia, Vuex | NgRx, Signals | Stores |

### 21.2 When to Choose Lit

| Choose Lit When | Choose React/Vue/Angular When |
|-----------------|-------------------------------|
| Building a component library | Building a full SPA with complex state |
| Components need to work across frameworks | Need a large ecosystem of libraries |
| Performance is critical (minimal JS) | Team is already experienced with the framework |
| You want to use web standards | Need mature SSR solutions |
| Micro-frontends architecture | Need mobile apps (React Native, etc.) |
| Design system / web component library | Complex routing and data management |
| Progressive enhancement | Need extensive tooling out-of-the-box |

