## 24. BEST PRACTICES

### 24.1 Component Design

| Practice | Details |
|----------|---------|
| **One component per file** | Keep components in separate files for maintainability |
| **Prefix tag names** | Use a prefix for your components: `my-button`, `app-header` |
| **Declare global types** | Add to `HTMLElementTagNameMap` for TypeScript |
| **Use @state for internal** | Never expose UI-only state as public attributes |
| **Immutable updates** | Always create new references for objects/arrays |
| **Small render methods** | Break complex templates into helper methods |
| **Colocate styles** | Keep styles in the same file as the component |
| **Document CSS parts** | Document `::part()` names and custom properties |

### 24.2 Performance

| Practice | Details |
|----------|---------|
| **Static styles** | Always prefer `static styles = css\`...\`` over inline `<style>` |
| **`nothing` over `''`** | Use `nothing` sentinel for empty conditionals |
| **Avoid unnecessary attributes** | Use `attribute: false` for complex data |
| **Event delegation** | Use on container, check target — for large lists |
| **Lazy load** | Dynamically import heavy child components |
| **Debounce rapid updates** | Batch property changes to reduce re-renders |

### 24.3 Accessibility (a11y)

```typescript
@customElement('a11y-button')
export class A11yButton extends LitElement {
  @property({ type: Boolean, reflect: true }) disabled = false;
  @property() label = '';

  static styles = css`
    :host { display: inline-block; }
    button:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid blue; outline-offset: 2px; }
  `;

  render() {
    return html`
      <button
        part="button"
        ?disabled=${this.disabled}
        aria-label=${this.label || nothing}
        aria-disabled=${this.disabled}
        role="button"
        tabindex=${this.disabled ? -1 : 0}
        @click=${this._onClick}
        @keydown=${this._onKeyDown}
      >
        <slot></slot>
      </button>
    `;
  }

  private _onClick(e: Event) {
    if (this.disabled) {
      e.preventDefault();
      e.stopPropagation();
      return;
    }
    this.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('button-click', { bubbles: true, composed: true }));
  }

  private _onKeyDown(e: KeyboardEvent) {
    if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') {
      e.preventDefault();
      this._onClick(e);
    }
  }
}
```

